INT. SUBMARINE BAY - COLD STORAGE - NIGHT

Frost on steel. Rows of crates under a single caged bulb. Breath hangs in the air like smoke.

A SENTRY (30s, parka, rifle slung) paces the aisle. He stops at a crate. Pries the lid with a gloved hand. Peers in.

From behind a stack of pallets, a second man watches him. THE TECHNICIAN (40s, thin, ID badge turned inward). He holds a small black box in one hand, thumb hovering over a button.

The Sentry sets down the lid. Turns. Looks directly at the pallets. The Technician holds his breath.

SENTRY
Hello?

No reply. The Sentry steps closer. Sniffs. Reaches for his radio.

SENTRY (CONT'D)
(into radio)
Control, I have movement in cold storage.

CONTROL (V.O.)
(over radio)
Confirm.

SENTRY
Possible. He's behind the pallets. He's not answering.

CONTROL (V.O.)
Hold position. Backup in two minutes.

The Sentry unslings his rifle. The Technician presses against the crate. A drop of sweat freezes on his forehead.

SENTRY
(low)
Come out. He won't hurt you.

The Technician closes his eyes. His thumb tightens. The box clicks.

Overhead, every light in the bay goes dark. In the black, a scuffle: boots on steel, a grunt, a shout, a rifle butt striking something hard. The caged bulb swings back on.

Both men stand, five feet apart. The Sentry's rifle points at the Technician. The Technician's box points at the Sentry. Neither lowers it.

SENTRY (CONT'D)
Put it down. He's got backup coming.

TECHNICIAN
(through his teeth)
So does he.

Somewhere above them, a muffled thump. A second. The ceiling trembles. Frost sifts from the pipes.

They look up together.
